<section class="brain-spine-section" style="background:#f8f9fa">
  <h2 class="brain-spine-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
  <div class="brain-spine-divider"></div>
  <div class="pt-faq" style="max-width:800px;margin:0 auto">
    <details><summary>What is the Ayurvedic approach to lumbar spondylosis treatment?</summary><p class="faq-a">Ayurveda addresses the imbalance and tissue depletion contributing to degenerative change in the lower spine rather than the pain alone. At KSAC Hospitals the approach begins with a precise diagnosis, including a review of the patient's X-ray or MRI reports and a neurological examination, after which the treating doctor prepares a customised plan. Depending on the case that plan may combine physician-supervised therapy, internal Ayurvedic medicines and structured mobility and strengthening guidance.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Will I be given the same treatment as other lumbar spondylosis patients?</summary><p class="faq-a">No. The plan depends on which levels are affected, how advanced the degeneration is, whether a nerve is involved and what the patient's occupation and posture demand of their back. Two patients with similar reports may still be advised different plans. The treating doctor decides after diagnosis and explains the plan before treatment begins.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Do I need to bring my X-ray or MRI to the consultation?</summary><p class="faq-a">Yes, where available. X-rays, MRI or CT reports, along with current prescriptions and records of earlier treatment, help the doctor arrive at a precise diagnosis and plan accordingly. <a href="/pages/ayurvedic-lumbar-spondylosis-treatment-in-hyderabad" style="color:#3c8dbc">Ayurvedic treatment for lumbar spondylosis</a> at KSAC Hospitals is planned around clinical findings and the patient's own reports and fresh imaging is advised only where it is needed.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is lumbar spondylosis the same as a slipped disc?</summary><p class="faq-a">No. Lumbar spondylosis refers to age-related degenerative change across the discs, vertebrae and spinal joints, while a <a href="/pages/ayurvedic-slip-disc-treatment-in-hyderabad" style="color:#3c8dbc">disc herniation</a>, commonly called a slipped disc, involves disc material pushing beyond its normal boundary. The two may coexist, since a degenerated disc is more prone to herniation. KSAC Hospitals assesses and treats each separately so the plan matches the actual diagnosis.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can Ayurvedic treatment manage lumbar spondylosis long term?</summary><p class="faq-a">Ongoing management is an important part of care for a degenerative condition. Ayurvedic lumbar spondylosis treatment in Hyderabad at KSAC Hospitals supports long-term management through periodic review, prescribed medicines where indicated, mobility practices and lifestyle guidance. The doctor monitors progress at follow-up and adjusts the plan as needs change. <a href="/pages/evidence-based-ayurveda" style="color:#3c8dbc">Evidence based Ayurveda in Hyderabad</a> at KSAC Hospitals means those decisions are guided by clinical assessment at each stage rather than a fixed schedule.</p></details>
    <details><summary>When should I seek urgent assessment rather than planned treatment?</summary><p class="faq-a">Progressive weakness in the legs, numbness around the inner thighs, groin or saddle area or any change in bladder or bowel control needs immediate medical assessment. These can indicate serious compression of the nerves at the base of the spine and are not suitable for conservative or elective care. Severe pain following a fall or injury also warrants prompt assessment.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What lifestyle changes support lumbar spondylosis management?</summary><p class="faq-a">Regular spinal mobility work, correct lifting and bending technique, avoiding long unbroken periods of sitting, maintaining a healthy body weight and using seating that supports the natural curve of the lower back all help. The treating doctor at KSAC Hospitals provides individualised guidance based on the patient's spinal status and occupational demands.</p></details>
  </div>
</section>

